                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 326.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Extract from Der Bund, Berne, January</hi> 10,
                    1881.</head>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schwytz</hi>.—The citizens of Gersau appear inclined
                    to solve the social question through a possible assistance to emigration. The
                    commune recently adopted a resolution to furnish every citizen who would
                    emigrate, who had attained his eighteenth year, 250 francs for his journey;
                    citizens from ten to eighteen years receive 100 francs; for children under ten
                    years of age an allowance of 30 francs is reckoned.</p>
            </div>
